{
  "name": "Injectors",
  "icon": "draconicevolution:wyvern_crafting_injector",
  "category": "draconicevolution:fusion_crafting",
  "sortnum": 2,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Injectors hold the ingredients of a fusion recipe, one stack each. There are four tiers:$(li)$(item)Draconium$() (basic)$(li)$(item)Wyvern$()$(li)$(item)Draconic$()$(li)$(item)Chaotic$()"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Every recipe has a tier, shown in JEI. $(l)Every injector that holds an item$() must be that tier or higher, or the core reports that the injector tier is too low. Lower-tier injectors can stay in the setup as long as they are empty.$(br2)Higher tiers also charge and craft faster."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "title": "Using injectors",
      "text": "Right-click an injector with an item to insert it; right-click again with an empty hand to take it back.$(br2)$(l)Shift-right-click$() with an empty hand toggles $(l)single item mode$(). In that mode the injector accepts only one item, which stops automation from overfilling it. Stack mode is the default."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:crafting",
      "recipe": "draconicevolution:machines/basic_crafting_injector",
      "text": "The basic injector, crafted normally."
    },
